# text
# c1: src/interchange.rs::SCHEMA_VERSION
seg-73e2bca0310d = <b>Semantic Versioning.</b> Pre-1.0 the scenario/result schema may change; breaking changes are called out, and the interchange schema version (<c1/>) is the single source of truth for artifact compatibility.

# text
# c1: cargo publish
# c2: CONTRIBUTING.md
seg-71cace8b6144 = <b>Release authority.</b> Publishing (e.g. <c1/>) is a manual maintainer step requiring a registry token. CI and the tag-gated Release workflow <b>never</b> publish to external registries automatically — they only re-run all checks and attach a build artifact. See <c2/> → Commits and versioning.

